\pard\plain\f1\fs28\b 12. Learning Outcomes\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs22\b0 After completing the case study, the student is expected to:\par
- Understand scheduling and process management concepts.\par
- Apply synchronization and deadlock handling techniques to real-life systems.\par
- Analyze resource allocation and evaluate system performance.\par
- Relate theoretical OS knowledge to domain-specific application problems.\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs28\b 13. Conclusion\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs22\b0 This case study demonstrates how operating system principles can be applied to a practical hospital management system. By incorporating scheduling, synchronization, deadlock prevention, and resource optimization, the design improves system reliability and service quality. Such a case study helps students understand the importance of operating systems in real-world engineering systems and connects course learning to societal and technical needs.\par
